  "body": "Please see the original Chromium bug report:\r\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1209102#c7\r\n\r\nIn short: Clicking a tel or mail protocol handler link in chromium triggers the 'beforeunload' event.\r\n\r\nThe question has now become whether or not this behaviour is desired or not according to the HTML specification itself. I personally believe it shouldn't, as a tel or mail protocol handler link doesn't actually trigger a page unload, unless there are reasons as to why it needs to do that.",
